Lojban isn't clearly of one order or the other, since it treats sets and pr=
operties and the like on a par with tree and dogs.  There is no particular =
problem in grammar or vocabulary to treating properties of predicates and q=
uantification over them.  There are some arguments about the correct way to=
 express a predicate as an argument, but that seems to revolve around just =
what a predicate is in Lojban ontology.  All the answers yield grammatical =
and intelligible results, though sometimes different ones.  None of them se=
em particularly stilted, but I haven't seen enough cases to get a feel for =
that.

Sent from my iPad

